# OS clutter
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Scratch files from local testing (the __ prefix is used for throwaway pages)
__*.html

# Local secrets for `netlify dev`. The deployed site reads its keys from
# Netlify's own environment variables; this file is only ever on one machine
# and must not reach the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# What `tools/publish.sh` assembles for a deploy. Generated, never edited.
_site/

# Netlify CLI state
.netlify/

# Photographic working folders. These are big — 291MB and 69MB — and they are
# inputs, not outputs: everything the site serves has already been cut from
# them into assets/images, which IS tracked. Committing them would take the
# repository past 700MB and make every clone painful, for files that only ever
# exist on the machine the photography is processed on. Back them up outside
# git.
NEW HAMPER PHOTOS/
Final upload/

# "Hamper Photos" (52MB) stays tracked: it is the original master set, small
# enough to carry, and the one thing that could not be recreated.
